[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m We need to find the perimeter of one of these triangles. The perimeter \( P \) of a right triangle is the sum of the lengths of its three sides. The two legs are each \( \frac{7\sqrt{2}}{2} \) inches, and the hypotenuse is the diagonal of the square, which is \( 7\sqrt{2} \) inches. Therefore, the perimeter is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
