[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the fold line is the diagonal of the square. The diagonal of a square with side length \( s \) is given by \( s\sqrt{2} \). For our square with side length 7 inches, the diagonal is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \text{Diagonal} = 7\sqrt{2} \text{ inches}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m When the square is unfolded, the diagonal becomes the hypotenuse of two congruent right triangles. Each of these triangles has legs that are half the side length of the original square, which is 3.5 inches. The hypotenuse of each triangle is the diagonal of the square, which is \( 7\sqrt{2} \) inches. We can verify this using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
