[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Now, we need to find the perimeter of one of these triangles. The perimeter of a right triangle is the sum of the lengths of its three sides. The two legs of the triangle are each 3.5 inches, and the hypotenuse is \( 7\sqrt{2} \) inches. Therefore, the perimeter is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \text{Perimeter} = 3.5 + 3.5 + 7\sqrt{2} = 7 + 7\sqrt{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Thus, the number of inches in the perimeter of one of these triangles is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
