[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the fold line is the perpendicular bisector of the diagonal of the square. This fold line creates two congruent right triangles. The diagonal of the square can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
