[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the fold line is the perpendicular bisector of the diagonal of the square. This fold line creates two congruent right triangles. The legs of each right triangle are half the length of the diagonal of the square.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m First, we calculate the length of the diagonal of the square. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the diagonal \(d\) of the square is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m d = \sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \sqrt{98} = 7\sqrt{2} \text{ inches}
