[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m [response] To find \(\cot 90^\circ\), we start by recalling the definition of the cotangent function. The cotangent of an angle \(\theta\) is the reciprocal of the tangent of that angle, i.e., \(\cot \theta = \frac{1}{\tan \theta}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m First, we need to determine \(\tan 90^\circ\). The tangent of an angle is defined as the ratio of the sine of the angle to the cosine of the angle, i.e., \(\tan \theta = \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m At \(90^\circ\), we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \sin 90^\circ = 1 \quad \text{and} \quad \cos 90^\circ = 0.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Therefore,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \tan 90^\circ = \frac{\sin 90^\circ}{\cos 90^\circ} = \frac{1}{0}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Since division by zero is undefined, \(\tan 90^\circ\) is undefined. Consequently, \(\cot 90^\circ = \frac{1}{\tan 90^\circ}\) is also undefined.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
