[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m [response] To determine the probability that the game will be won before the fourth turn, we first need to calculate the probability of winning on a single turn. A turn consists of rolling a standard die and tossing a fair coin. The probability of rolling a 1 or a 6 on the die is \(\frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3}\), and the probability of getting heads on the coin is \(\frac{1}{2}\). Therefore, the probability of winning on a single turn is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m P(\text{win on one turn}) = \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}
