[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m First, we factor the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ x^2 + x - 6 = (x + 3)(x - 2). \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m So, the function can be rewritten as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ y = \frac{2}{(x + 3)(x - 2)}. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m The denominator is zero when \( x = -3 \) or \( x = 2 \). These are the points where the function is undefined, and thus the vertical asymptotes occur at these points.
