[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m First, consider the range of \(\sin x\) for \(0^\circ < x < 180^\circ\). The sine function takes values in the interval \((0, 1]\) in this range. Therefore, \(\sqrt{\sin x}\) takes values in the interval \((0, 1)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Next, we need to determine the range of \( y = \log_2 (\sqrt{\sin x}) \). Since \(\sqrt{\sin x}\) ranges from \(0\) to \(1\) (excluding \(0\)), we need to find the corresponding range of the logarithm. Specifically, \(\log_2 (\sqrt{\sin x}) = \frac{1}{2} \log_2 (\sin x)\).
