[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m [response] Given the polynomial \( p(x) = x^2 + ax + b \) with roots \( 2a \) and \( b \), we can use Vieta's formulas which tell us that the sum of the roots is equal to the negation of the coefficient of \( x \) (i.e., \(-a\)) and the product of the roots is equal to the constant term (i.e., \( b \)). Therefore, we have:
