[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ y = \frac{1}{5 - x} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Then we substitute this into the expression we want to minimize:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ \frac{1}{x} + y = \frac{1}{x} + \frac{1}{5 - x} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Let \( f(x) = \frac{1}{x} + \frac{1}{5 - x} \). To find the critical points, we take the derivative and set it to zero:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ f'(x) = -\frac{1}{x^2} + \frac{1}{(5 - x)^2} = 0 \]
