[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ f(x) + f(y) \le 0 \quad \text{and} \quad f(x) - f(y) \le 0. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ x^2 + 6x + 1 + y^2 + 6y + 1 \le 0 \quad \text{and} \quad x^2 + 6x + 1 \le y^2 + 6y + 1. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m The first inequality simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ x^2 + y^2 + 6x + 6y + 2 \le 0. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m Completing the square, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ (x+3)^2 + (y+3)^2 \le 8. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m This is a circle centered at \((-3, -3)\) with radius \(\sqrt{8} = 2\sqrt{2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m The second inequality simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ x^2 + 6x + 1 \le y^2 + 6y + 1, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ x^2 - y^2 + 6x - 6y \le 0, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m or:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m \[ (x-y)(x+y+6) \le 0. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=42128)[0m This inequality describes the region between the lines \(x-y=0\) and \(x+y+6=0\).
